A||N||7||87ECO5||Suggestions for dogbone color||||5||
Z||000000||87ECO5||05-10-2001||06:44 PM||||I've got a stock dogbone from which I've removed the rubber bushings.  I purchased a set of poly replacements which are black in color.<P>I'm looking for suggestions on what color to paint the bone.  I am planning to dress up the entire engine bay so I kinda want to coordinate with other stuff in there.  I thought about black but thought the bone would get lost in all the other black in there.  I also thought about red (kind of a reverse "Ultimate" dogbone) but thought it would be too much red with the plenum, valve covers and strut tower brace.<P>I ended up spraying it last night with Krylon aluminum but it turned out looking cheap.  Though the color is called aluminum, the color turns out to be that "chrome-paint" color.  BLAH!!!!!<P>Looking for suggestions ...<P>TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||05-10-2001||06:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87ECO5:<BR><B>I've got a stock dogbone from which I've removed the rubber bushings.  I purchased a set of poly replacements which are black in color.<P>I'm looking for suggestions on what color to paint the bone.  I am planning to dress up the entire engine bay so I kinda want to coordinate with other stuff in there.  I thought about black but thought the bone would get lost in all the other black in there.  I also thought about red (kind of a reverse "Ultimate" dogbone) but thought it would be too much red with the plenum, valve covers and strut tower brace.<P>I ended up spraying it last night with Krylon aluminum but it turned out looking cheap.  Though the color is called aluminum, the color turns out to be that "chrome-paint" color.  BLAH!!!!!<P>Looking for suggestions ...<P>TIA</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> Where did you find black poly?? Ive been looking for them for a long time...<P>Thanks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><I>Haze</I><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">      </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A><BR><I>If you want to add your Fiero to the collection, post or send me a photo. (Sent photos ONLY to: purplehazeracing@yahoo.com )</I><P><A HREF="http://www.clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero Club</A>||||reg||11
Z||000002||Nashco||05-10-2001||07:26 PM||||You can get black poly from <A HREF="http://www.suspension.com/fiero-prothane.htm" TARGET=_blank>www.suspension.com</A>.  I just ordered the poly bushings for the dogbone from them, and was satisfied with customer service.  I haven't got the bushings in the mail yet, but I'm sure they will come fine, as they stock everything.  They were only 20 bucks plus shipping, and available in red or black.  I didn't think to ask if all of their bushings had that option, but I will definitely ask next time I use them.  Black would be good for suspension to look cleaner, but red would be good for knowing if it needs cleaning and for shows or anything.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||87ECO5||05-10-2001||08:16 PM||||Like Nashco stated,  <A HREF="http://Suspension.com" TARGET=_blank>Suspension.com</A>  stocks red or black.  I ordered their $340 "complete" '84-'87 suspension restoration kit.  It included six ball joints, four tie rod ends, two tie rod end dust boots, two sway bar end links, and poly bushings for control arms, sway bar, cradle and dogbone.<P>Now, here's the catcher:  when I was ordering the kit, I asked for red.  But, when the person on the other end of the phone told me the black color was graphite-impregnated (anti-squeak), I went with that instead.||||reg||1
